    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d636">

                <pb facs="0742" n="732" sameAs="frus:frus1942China/pg732"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.0011 Pacific War/2664</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Gauss</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 477</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Chungking</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1942-06-22">June 22,
                        1942</date>.<lb/>[Received July 23.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to refer to recent
                    statements in the Chinese press, one of which—an editorial in the <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Ta Kung Pao</hi> of April 6—was brought to the attention
                    of the Department by my despatch no. 374 of April 16, 1942,<anchor n="4"
                        xml:id="d636-f1"/> to the effect that the Liu Chiu Islands would be
                    separated from Japan in the peace settlement, and to enclose a copy of a
                    memorandum of a conversation in which the Director of the Eastern Asiatic
                    Department of the Ministry of Foreign Affairs denied Chinese claims to the
                    Islands.</p>
                <p>Respectfully yours,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>C. E. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Gauss</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>


                <xi:include href="d636-a1.xml" xpointer="d636-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
